 of a Beta vulgaris subsp. vulgaris plant in the Conditiva Group. The plant is a root vegetable also known as the table beet, garden beet, or dinner beet, or else categorized by color as red beet or golden beet. Its leaves constitute a leaf vegetable called beet greens. It is native to the Azores, Western Europe to the Mediterranean and India."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-beetroot"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beetroot"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":11,"groups":[["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"],["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"],["Vinegret","dish/vinegret"]]],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"],["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Vinegret","dish/vinegret"]]],["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"]]],["Lithuanian cuisine","cuisine/lithuanian-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"]]],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine",[["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Vinegret","dish/vinegret"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"]]],["Latvian cuisine","cuisine/latvian-cuisine",[["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"]]],["Moldovan cuisine","cuisine/moldovan-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"]]],["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine",[["Borscht","dish/borscht"]]],["Slovak cuisine","cuisine/slovak-cuisine",[["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beta vulgaris","ingredient/beta-vulgaris"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Brassica oleracea","ingredient/brassica-oleracea"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Kefir","ingredient/kefir"],["Kvass","ingredient/kvass"],["Sorrel","ingredient/sorrel"],["Beta","ingredient/beta"],["Clupea","ingredient/clupea"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Herring","ingredient/herring"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Horseradish","ingredient/horseradish"],["Beet","ingredient/beet"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/a/ae/Detroitdarkredbeets.png/500px-Detroitdarkredbeets.png","w":500,"h":752,"by":"BriannaWalther","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detroitdarkredbeets.png"}},"dish/conti-roll":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/conti-roll","n":"Conti roll","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The conti roll, or continental roll, is a sandwich popular in Perth, Western Australia. It was originally referred to by local native speakers of Italian as a panino Italiano. Its Anglophone name alludes to continental Europe (as opposed to the British Isles), the source of the majority of its ingredients."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-conti-roll"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conti_roll"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Food preservation","ingredient/food-preservation"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromital