dients","count":1,"links":[["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"China Sichuan Food","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"chinasichuanfood.com","note":"Elaine's blog of Chinese home recipes with a strong Sichuan focus.","url":"https://www.chinasichuanfood.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"The Mala Market Blog","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"blog.themalamarket.com","note":"Recipes and ingredient guides from a US importer of Sichuan pantry staples.","url":"https://blog.themalamarket.com/mala-market-blog-about-page/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Sichuan cuisine","links":[["Doubanjiang","dish/doubanjiang"],["Fish with pickled mustard greens","dish/fish-with-pickled-mustard-greens"],["Laziji","dish/laziji"],["Suan la fen","dish/suan-la-fen"],["Yuxiang shredded pork","dish/yuxiang-shredded-pork"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/f3/Kuanfen_noodles.jpg/500px-Kuanfen_noodles.jpg","w":500,"h":503,"by":"8UB3RG1N3","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kuanfen_noodles.jpg"}},"ingredient/quark":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/quark","n":"Quark","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["Quark or quarg (sometimes translated as curd cheese) is a type of fresh dairy product made from milk. The milk is soured, usually by adding lactic acid bacteria cultures, and strained once the desired curdling is achieved. It can be classified as fresh acid-set cheese. Traditional quark can be made without rennet, but in modern dairies small quantities of rennet are typically added. It is soft, white and unaged, and usually has no salt added."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-quark"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quark_(dairy_product)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[