to western and southern Asia. It has been cultivated since ancient times and is now widely grown throughout the world. Ficus carica is the type species of the genus Ficus, which comprises over 800 tropical and subtropical plant species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-fig"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fig_fruit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Peruvian cuisine","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine",[["Picarones","dish/picarones"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Rakı","dish/rak"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Figs","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":1328067,"top":[["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",344200],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",229936],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",124685],["Algeria","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",113843],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",73294],["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",51732],["Afghanistan","cuisine/afghan-cuisine",46747],["Syria","cuisine/syrian-cuisine",40370],["Uzbekistan","cuisine/uzbek-cuisine",29461],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",28169],["Saudi Arabia","cuisine/saudi-arabian-cuisine",27725],["Albania","cuisine/cuisine-of-albania",23078],["Tunisia","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine",23012],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",20282],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",14751]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chancaca","ingredient/chancaca"],["Cucurbita maxima","ingredient/cucurbita-maxima"],["Panela","ingredient/panela"],["Squash (plant)","ingredient/squash-plant"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Barrel","ingredient/barrel"],["Date","ingredient/date"],["Grape","ingredient/grape"],["Pomace","ingredient/pomace"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/2e/Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg/500px-Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg","w":500,"h":767,"by":"Trew, C.J","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg"}},"dish/thua-nao":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/thua-nao","n":"Thua nao","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Thua nao, also known as pè bok (Burmese: ပဲပုပ်; lit. 'rotten beans'), is a fermented soybean product used in Burmese and Thai cuisine, particularly by the Shan, Tai Lue, and Northern Thai peoples as a cooking ingredient or condiment. Thua nao is created by fermenting cooked soybeans with naturally occurring microbes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-thua-nao"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thua_nao"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Burmese cuisine","cuisine/burmese-cuisine"],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Hot Thai Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"hot-thai-kitchen.com","note":"Pailin Chongchitnant's recipes and videos, with background on technique and ingredients.","url":"https://hot-thai-kitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"SheSimmers","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"shesimmers.com","note":"Bangkok-born writer Leela Punyaratabandhu's blog on Thai home cooking.","url":"https://shesimmers.com/who-is-shesimmers","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Burmese cuisine","links":[["Burmese salads","dish/burmese-salads"],["Khao soi","dish/khao-soi"],["Mohinga","dish/mohinga"],["Thali","dish/thali"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/4/45/2017_0419_Thanin_market_tua_nao.jpg/500px-2017_0419_Thanin_market_tua_nao.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Takeaway","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2017_0419_Thanin_market_tua_nao.jpg"}}}